A||||11||Greg Piet||Anyone know the specs on no catalytic?||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||12-06-2000||01:25 AM||||Just to keep the EPA happy, this question is posed for racing/off road application only.<P>If one has unrestriced the stock exhaust manifolds and then removed the catalytic converter on a V6 stock 2.8, what would be the performance upgrade...  I know that unrestricting the 13b Mazda rotary exhaust (headers/no cats) greatly improved the performance of the hamster motors by 30hp on the low end (at least accd. to "private" dyno tests).||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||12-06-2000||03:45 AM||||you gain some horsepower, and lose some torque.  Get a much better sound, too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||12-06-2000||08:12 AM||||I believe Travis(1FST2M6) said it lost 8lbs of torque on my car(correct me if I'm wrong Trav.)  I considered putting a cat back on when he told me, but with the headers and flomaster is sounds downright evil.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||12-06-2000||10:38 AM||||your right Jeff... it's sounds too sweet to care about the torque loss!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  the gain in upper RPM HP isn't really usable but there was a gain (3-4hp at 5800rpm)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gold87SE||12-06-2000||01:36 PM||||I got the ocelot performance exhaust and put on a straight pipe and it sounds SWEET!||||reg||1
Z||000005||loafer87gt||12-06-2000||04:08 PM||||Trav, when I boought my car used the cat was alredy cut out, I added in a "cherry bomb" boom tube where the cat used to be to quiet things down a bit. If I got a hi-po cat, would i notice any gains? Do you really lose 8 ft torque by removing it?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Greg Piet||12-06-2000||05:34 PM||||Uhh not to be a killjoy, but how does the sound improve performance?  Intimidation factor????<P>So in essence getting rid of the cat hinders performance although it definatley frees up the exhaust?||||reg||1
Z||000007||MikeE||12-06-2000||05:43 PM||||Did it actually lose torque or did the torque peak just move up the RPM band, resulting in an 8 lb-ft loss at its former torque peak RPM?<P>I don't see how less restriction could result in a torque loss unless the engine could't be tuned enough to compensate for the change.  If that's the case then further mods down the road will gain back the torque loss and then some.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||12-07-2000||08:23 AM||||i'll go down to the shop at lunch and print out the dyno sheet. the peak only droped at 3lbft but from 1800-2600 i lost 8 full lbft! the peaks did shift up on the rpm range. (not as bad as the headers) but still shifted. as for the noise.. yeah.. just intimidation... it works for Mustangs!||||reg||1
Z||000009||msweldon||12-07-2000||09:22 AM||||If your into as much performance out of the stock exhaust as possible, leave it alone, port the stock manifolds if anything.  I have a true dual setup with no CATs w/ glasspacks.  Sounds very mean, however, there is a noticeable loss in low-end.  I don't have any numbers, but it is more than noticeable. Its extremely easy to rev which adds a bit of fun to sport driving, but the stock 2.8 "needs" the back pressure provided by the stock exhaust.<P>If you go with a stroked 2.8 or a 3.4 the exhaust mods might work well.<P>mw||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jackalrr||12-07-2000||03:35 PM||||Would it be worth it to go with the Borla stainless exhaust (like $534) over the ocelot performance from the fiero store?<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<BR>-----<BR>jackalrr@cinci.rr.com||||reg||1
Z||000011||1FST2M6||12-07-2000||04:08 PM||||for the performance gain vs cost NO.. take your car to a local muffler shop and have them mandrel bend a new exhaust 2.5". Brullen, Powertone, dynomax, Flomaster all make nice stuff.. and for about 1/2 the price of the prefab unit. ||||reg||1
